2026-08-25T00:00:17Z (SITE66606-1) 'unused
 # tags: site:section
 Text:Site1  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:18Z (SITE66606-1) 'A serial nothing was ever written under. These three sat in neither register: not allocated to a document, and not retired from one, so a reader counting the live rows saw a gap and had nothing telling them what it meant. Recorded so the gap reads as a decision rather than as a loss. A satellite relation rather than an empty slug on the spine, because a serial with no document is a different fact from a serial with one, and CLAUDE.md's normal form takes satellites over nullable columns. NOTE THE LIMIT: `check-rfd-serials.py` keys on the scope names Allocated and Deleted and skips this one, so nothing enforces these. What prevents reuse is RFD 1000's rule that a new serial is the next unused one, which is max plus one and never a gap.
 # tags: site:section-note
 Text:Site1  1 LINE
 Text:Written

